\title{gamlssPosthoc: Marginal and Distributional Post-Hoc Inference for GAMLSS}
\description{
Tools for post-hoc inference after generalized additive models for location,
scale and shape (GAMLSS). The package treats the estimand, target population,
comparison scale, and uncertainty method as separate choices. It routes
supported parameter-wise requests to \code{emmeans} or \code{marginaleffects} and uses
full predictive distributions plus refit bootstrap for zero-adjusted,
smoother-based, and multi-parameter targets.
}
\section{Main functions}{

\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=gamlss_posthoc]{gamlss_posthoc()}} computes standardized estimates and scientific contrasts.
\item \code{\link[=gamlss_posthoc_plan]{gamlss_posthoc_plan()}} diagnoses model capabilities and recommends an engine.
\item \code{\link[=gamlss_trend]{gamlss_trend()}} evaluates curves, derivatives, turning points, and optima.
\item \code{\link[=gamlss_distribution_summary]{gamlss_distribution_summary()}} summarizes ordinary and zero-adjusted distributions.
\item \code{\link[=gamlss_poly_compare]{gamlss_poly_compare()}} compares already-fitted nested polynomial models.
\item \code{\link[=gamlss_engine_info]{gamlss_engine_info()}} provides a compact legacy routing summary.
\item \code{\link[=gamlss_cld]{gamlss_cld()}} adds optional compact-letter displays to pairwise results.
}
